<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:48:22 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>Scorching summer takes toll on bees and honey harvests in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-scorching-summer-takes-toll-on-bees-and-honey-harvests-in-france</link><description>
France produces 20,000 tonnes of honey each year, but successive heatwaves and persistent drought across Europe this summer are impacting bee populations as flowering plants dry out and colonies struggle to find food. Beekeeper Romain Lacotte and his family farm 1,000 hives in Haute-Corrèze, central France, an area considered one of the country's natural water towers. But even there, he tells RFI, high temperatures and lack of rain are taking their toll.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11563ee0-9ae1-11f1-bfbb-0f799d11d84e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:44:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg">© ASSOCIATED PRESS - Jacquelyn Martin </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC and M23 rebels agree on roadmap for peace in eastern Congo</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-drc-and-m23-rebels-agree-on-roadmap-for-peace-in-eastern-congo</link><description>
The Democratic Republic of Congo government and the M23 rebel group have agreed on a roadmap for peace talks aimed at resolving the protracted conflict in eastern DRC. It marks the latest step in an internationally brokered peace process that has seen the parties make cautious concessions, without ending the fighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8dd2067c-9ef4-11f1-b3c6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177576707008.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8dd2067c-9ef4-11f1-b3c6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177576707008.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">57463c2a-9ef6-11f1-9684-4b4489a4c262</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:00:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8dd2067c-9ef4-11f1-b3c6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177576707008.jpg">© AP Photo/Moses Sawasawa</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Saudi crown prince heads to France as Paris seeks closer Gulf ties</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-saudi-crown-prince-heads-to-france-as-paris-seeks-closer-gulf-ties</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron will host Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman on Sunday for a two-day official visit, as Paris looks to deepen ties with Riyadh against a backdrop of war in the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">128f22b8-9d66-11f1-be58-479c257d485f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 07:05:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg">© AP - Michel Euler </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Mystery elephant deaths in Kenya leave experts divided over cause</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-mystery-elephant-deaths-in-kenya-leave-experts-divided-over-cause</link><description>
Conservationists and Maasai communities are calling for urgent answers as paralysis-like symptoms spread among elephants in Kenya's Amboseli National Park, with competing theories emerging over what is causing their deaths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38c7617a-9bd1-11f1-889b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Genghis-Khan-Elephant-Kenya.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38c7617a-9bd1-11f1-889b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Genghis-Khan-Elephant-Kenya.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6595647c-9bcc-11f1-8fd9-dfc10b227463</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:13:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38c7617a-9bd1-11f1-889b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Genghis-Khan-Elephant-Kenya.jpg">© SIMON MAINA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Togo says it has 'serious' evidence against detained French journalists</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-togo-says-it-has-serious-evidence-against-detained-french-journalists</link><description>
Togo's government says it has "serious and consistent evidence" against two French documentary filmmakers detained since July on charges of making false statements. Gaël Mocaër and Sebastian Perez Pezzani were arrested along with their Togolese fixer, Fred Vedomey, and have denied wrongdoing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdddc9cc-9ec9-11f1-9875-e5f10da2b52b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:56:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg">© AFP/EMILE KOUTON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Southern African mothers plead for sons lured to Russia's war in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260823-southern-african-mothers-plead-for-sons-lured-to-russia-s-war</link><description>
Instead of celebrating her son's birthday this month, Zimbabwean mother Rodwin Chitewere spent the day praying for his body to be brought home from Russia, where he was reportedly killed fighting Moscow's war against Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3108037c-9b90-11f1-8781-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/4f0ee42d48be3951fcc0a4d769636323e1b83893.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3108037c-9b90-11f1-8781-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/4f0ee42d48be3951fcc0a4d769636323e1b83893.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a3badee-9bb2-11f1-9818-f5b8caecbf68</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:28:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3108037c-9b90-11f1-8781-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/4f0ee42d48be3951fcc0a4d769636323e1b83893.jpg">© RAJESH JANTILAL / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>'Niu Lai', the 'so bad it's good' Chinese cartoon becoming a box-office hit</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/culture/20260823-niu-lai-the-so-bad-chinese-animated-film-breaking-box-office-records</link><description>
An amateur animated film has become a surprise box-office hit in China, fuelling a wider debate about cinema, artificial intelligence and audience tastes. Made by a mother-and-son team on a shoestring budget, Niu Lai went from commercial failure to viral sensation after attracting a wave of negative reviews.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/76714c20-9bcc-11f1-a359-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/niu-lai.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/76714c20-9bcc-11f1-a359-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/niu-lai.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c66969a-9c7c-11f1-a91e-c5f434e2bfee</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 10:15:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/76714c20-9bcc-11f1-a359-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/niu-lai.png">© Dalian Jingyuan Culture Film and Television Media</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eroding coastlines unearth and destroy slave graves in French Caribbean</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-eroding-coastlines-unearth-and-destroy-slave-graves-in-french-caribbean</link><description>
Rising seas and coastal erosion are exposing the graves of enslaved people on beaches in the French Caribbean departments of Martinique and Guadeloupe, bringing long-buried remains back into view. Archaeologists say the retreating coastline is revealing new information about people who were enslaved centuries ago, but also destroying sites of historical and cultural importance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a0474c0-9a39-11f1-8ac6-db7960a1f159</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:07:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg">© Thomas Romon / Inrap</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France to send interceptor missiles to Ukraine after Russian strikes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260822-france-to-send-interceptor-missiles-to-ukraine-after-russian-strikes</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Saturday announced Paris would deliver new interceptor missiles to Ukraine, with Kyiv's air defences running short after the latest round of deadly Russian attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ba90ba6-9d7e-11f1-ad58-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T192414Z-1904355796-RC2H2NACS2W0-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ba90ba6-9d7e-11f1-ad58-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T192414Z-1904355796-RC2H2NACS2W0-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7339d4d2-9e2e-11f1-8d94-efa8280ce22b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:52:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ba90ba6-9d7e-11f1-ad58-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T192414Z-1904355796-RC2H2NACS2W0-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Oleksandr Ratushniak / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ravaged by wildfires, France's Fontainebleau forest reopens to public</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-france-s-fontainebleau-forest-reopens-to-public-after-wildfires</link><description>
The forest of Fontainebleau outside Paris has partially reopened to the public after remaining off-limits for over a month due to devastating wildfires. From Saturday, visitors can access some 80 percent of the forest, but are being warned to show caution around fragile wildlife and charred trees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b21100-9e04-11f1-bb3d-976fc488f692</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg">© AFP - SIMON WOHLFAHRT </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Diplomats urge France and UK to uphold rule of law in Palestinian territories</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260822-former-envoys-urge-joint-french-uk-action-on-palestinian-territories</link><description>
Dozens of former senior French and UK diplomats on Saturday urged their governments to work together to uphold international law in the Palestinian territories, accusing Israel of seeking to "destroy" any prospect of a viable Palestinian state.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f01b776-9e0e-11f1-b29d-1df8a6684097</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:46:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg">© Ilia YEFIMOVICH / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Still waters run deep: why Palme d'or winner 'Fjord' questions our certainties</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/culture/20260822-why-palme-d-or-winner-fjord-questions-our-certainties-cristian-mungiu-interview</link><description>
An isolated village in Norway sees its peaceful veneer upset by the arrival of a new family in Fjord, the Palme d'Or-winning film released in French cinemas this week. Inspired by real-life cases, Romanian director Cristian Mungiu explores questions of domestic violence, religion, culture and tolerance through a story that asks whose version of the truth can be trusted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d308978-5308-11f1-b3f1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/204424-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d308978-5308-11f1-b3f1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/204424-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a886d300-9bd2-11f1-be57-bfebf5b206b8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:05:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d308978-5308-11f1-b3f1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/204424-2.jpg">© Why Not Productions</source><dc:creator>Ollia Horton with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French farmers dip into winter fodder as drought leaves pastures bare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-french-farmers-dip-into-winter-fodder-as-drought-leaves-pastures-bare</link><description>
Repeated heatwaves and drought have made it a punishing summer for French farmers – scorching pastures, straining livestock and driving up costs. With grass disappearing from fields, cattle farmers across the country are already dipping into fodder meant to feed their herds through winter.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44161466-9d40-11f1-9260-c93d65df09a9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 07:04:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg">© Zeenat Hansrod</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo Ebola outbreak 'growing exponentially' with more than 2,500 dead</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-dr-congo-ebola-outbreak-growing-exponentially-with-more-than-2-500-dead</link><description>
The Ebola outbreak raging in the Democratic Republic of Congo is growing "exponentially", with more than 2,500 deaths recorded and half of those in the last 20 days, the senior UN coordinator on the disease said Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">837f67ba-9d54-11f1-9288-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:36:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg">© Jospin Mwisha / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Turkey, Saudi Arabia and Pakistan strengthen ties as Israel tensions rise</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260822-turkey-saudi-arabia-and-pakistan-strengthen-ties-as-israel-tensions-rise</link><description>
Tensions between Turkey and Israel have intensified after an Israeli airstrike targeted a Syrian military airbase near the Turkish border. The strike came days after Turkey’s new military pact with Saudi Arabia and Pakistan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d4b7ad0e-9255-11f1-9f2e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-07T111511Z-1176211354-RC2NTMA0W6QT-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-DEFENCE-AGREEMENT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d4b7ad0e-9255-11f1-9f2e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-07T111511Z-1176211354-RC2NTMA0W6QT-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-DEFENCE-AGREEMENT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39ae4a06-9d55-11f1-9576-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 08:07:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France backs down on plan to make patients pay more for healthcare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260821-france-backs-down-on-plan-to-make-patients-pay-more-for-healthcare-medicine</link><description>
The French government has scrapped plans to double the annual ceiling on out-of-pocket charges for medicines, medical appointments and other healthcare, after criticism from patient groups and health professionals. The cap was due to rise from €100 to €200, but the government will instead pursue a smaller increase linked to inflation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">264a2d16-9d52-11f1-8885-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:45:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg">AP - Daniel Cole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and European allies press Israel to abandon West Bank settlement plan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-france-and-european-allies-press-israel-to-abandon-west-bank-settlement-plan</link><description>
France has joined Germany, Italy and the United Kingdom in calling on Israel to halt the expansion of settlements illegal under international law in the occupied West Bank, and immediately withdraw tenders issued this week for more than 1,200 new homes under the controversial E1 project.
